# Fast Linux Host iteration

The operator approved a component-first iteration path and Host compiler-output
caching after a small Native10 change repeatedly waited on full package builds.
Branch `host-build-iteration` is based on the complete `native10-buffer-reuse`
candidate. It preserves that work; GPU-resident capture remains deferred.

## Two explicit paths

`bash scripts/ci/dispatch.sh linux-native10-tests false` compiles the actual
Native10 headers and hardware-only probes on a disposable Rocky 9.7 worker.
Only GCC 14, sanitizer libraries, XCB declarations and the exact pinned CUDA
declaration headers are needed. The job does not prepare FFmpeg, Boost, Rust,
the encoder application or a package. It runs normal/sanitized tests and the
real Host version-policy fixture, then exports probes with exact source/hash
provenance. GPU probes still run only on authorized hardware; compilation is
not hardware or installed-session acceptance.

`bash scripts/ci/dispatch.sh linux-host false` remains the full candidate path.
It performs the complete integration, input, audio, transport and RPM checks.
None of those checks is skipped or weakened by a successful component run.
For an explicitly component-only experiment, a `[skip ci]` commit can suppress
automatic package jobs; dispatch the component workflow at the committed/pushed
SHA. PR and candidate qualification still require the full applicable gates.

## Compiler outputs

Host-only `sccache` is pinned to version 0.19.0 and its official archive SHA-256.
It is installed into job scratch after dependency bootstrap, never shipped.
CMake C/C++/CUDA launchers and Cargo's Rust wrapper cache eligible compilation
outputs. The qualified compiler choices, full CUDA architecture set, source
checks, clean build directories, final linking and test execution are preserved.
Uncacheable/linking operations continue normally. No CMake or Cargo build tree
is restored.

Snapshots have a 2 GiB bound and are saved only by successful trusted jobs.
The namespace includes the toolchain, CUDA recipe, cache policy and stable
builder paths; each compiler independently keys the source, headers and flags.
Changes to package versions/commits do not discard all compiler outputs.
Version metadata now affects only the two Host translation units that use it.
The version fixture verifies new runtime identity and unchanged video compiler
inputs across a version/commit change. Actual cache smoke checks require C++,
CUDA and Rust hits and reject stale values after a header change.

Ubuntu's existing compiler cache and every product's dependency cache are
unchanged. Cache restore remains branch/default-branch-scoped on GitHub; new
Host caching needs an initial population before a warm-build claim is valid.
`--clean-bootstrap` bypasses both dependency and compiler reuse.

## Qualification

Record the fast job's elapsed time and exported probe provenance, then compare
cold and warm complete Host jobs at the same source. Require actual cache-hit
statistics, all package gates and the correct visible/package version. Do not
promise a duration or infer correctness from a high hit rate alone.

Status: implementation and local policy/version fixtures are ready. Hosted fast
job and full cold/warm cache qualification are pending. Native10 buffer-only
candidate 1.4.13 passed its full build after one unchanged retry of an existing
zero-before-FEC-loss loopback assertion; retain that failure record separately.
